  "id": "COMPOUND:30070 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "Hippurin-1 is implicated in the biological activity of SMMC-7721 through a multi-step mechanism involving the target VMRC-LCP and Ginsenoside R10. The evidence suggests that Hippurin-1 acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of Ginsenoside R10, both of which ultimately interact with SMMC-7721. This pathway is supported by a consistent score of 0.5247 across three distinct paths, indicating a plausible and robust relationship. The involvement of VMRC-LCP and Ginsenoside R10 in the interaction with SMMC-7721 suggests a potential role in cellular processes that could be relevant to cancer biology. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of cellular targets, which may contribute to the observed effect on SMMC-7721. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Hippurin-1 influences SMMC-7721, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
